MOM:010220.canonicalSolution:
The midline encloses
\[
A_m=\pi r^2=\pi(0.05)^2=\boxed{0.0025\pi\ \text{m}^2}.
\]
Bredt's formula gives the circulating flow
\[
q
=\frac{T}{2A_m}
=\frac{1000}{2\cdot0.0025\pi}
=\frac{1000}{0.005\pi}
=\boxed{\frac{200000}{\pi}\ \text{N}/\text{m}}
=63.662\ \text{N}/\text{mm}.
\]
The wall shear is
\[
\tau
=\frac{q}{t}
=\frac{200000/\pi}{0.002}
=\frac{10^8}{\pi}\ \text{Pa}
=\boxed{\frac{100}{\pi}\ \text{MPa}}
=31.831\ \text{MPa}.
\]
The thin-wall torsion constant is
\[
J_t
=2\pi r^3 t
=2\pi(0.05)^3(0.002)
=2\pi\cdot1.25\times10^{-4}\cdot0.002
=\boxed{5\times10^{-7}\pi\ \text{m}^4}.
\]
The equivalent Bredt form $4A_m^2 t/\oint\mathrm{d}s$ with $\oint\mathrm{d}s=2\pi r=0.1\pi$ reproduces the same $J_t$. The twist is
\[
\theta
=\frac{TL}{GJ_t}
=\frac{1000\cdot2}{80\times10^9\cdot5\times10^{-7}\pi}
=\frac{2000}{4.00\times10^4\,\pi}
=\boxed{\frac{0.05}{\pi}\ \text{rad}}
=0.0159155\ \text{rad}
=\boxed{0.911891^\circ}.
\]

Sentence (i) is false: dropping the factor $2$ reports $q=400000/\pi$ N/m and $\tau=200/\pi$ MPa, twice the true shear. Sentence (ii) is false: a solid shaft of radius $r$ has $J=\pi r^4/2=3.125\times10^{-6}\pi$ m$^4$, six and one-quarter times $J_t$, and would twist by only $0.008/\pi$ rad.

The model is a single closed thin-walled cell in Saint-Venant torsion. It does not use an open-section warping constant, a bilinear law, a thermal twist, a beam field, Mohr's circle, or Euler buckling.

